# Disable end-of-line normalization repository-wide.
#
# The verification checkpoints under docs/checkpoints/ and work/checkpoints/
# record SHA-256 hashes of specific files as evidence, and the harness scripts
# re-verify staged inputs against those hashes at run time. If Git rewrote line
# endings on checkout, the bytes on disk would no longer match the recorded
# hashes and previously valid evidence would appear to have been tampered with.
# Storing every file byte-for-byte keeps those hashes meaningful.
* -text
